# Converted from the old Grade 2 Survex data (Grade2/Grade2/Out.svx).

# > Ogof Draenen: "Out" (part of Waterfall Series, off Upstream Passage)
# 
# This passage was called Out for want of a better name. It is really
# just another part of the Waterfall series.
# 
# BCRA Survey Grade: 3
# 
# Survey conducted on 21/1/96 Peter Bolt & Rich Blake.
# 
# Instrument		Name of operator		Serial Number
# ====================  ==============================  =====================
# Compass:
# Tape:
# Clinometer:
# Book:
# Data entry:		Tim Long

# Prime Survey Stations (describe location of permanent marks and note the tie-in
# point for any unsurveyed side passages)
# 
# Stations 1 == stn 1 of Yes passage (A. Garman 21/1/96)

# Specify name of survey section. One survey section per file. Don't forget to *End it.

survey out

# Station Equivalences - export all junction names here.

# Describe the units used and scale (if any).
# E.G. if measurements recorded in centimetres, *Units Length 0.01 metres

# Calibrate instruments (required to claim grade 5).
# The correction specified is subtracted from the readings. Note that
# tape calibration is a more reliable method of correcting for cut tapes
# than mentally adding the missing length in the cave.

# *Calibrate Tape 0	; Use this to correct for cut tapes.
# *Calibrate Compass 0	; Compass zero-error (different to declination).
# *Calibrate Clino 0     ; Clinometer zero-error.

# Magnetic North (declination) to Grid North correction
# Mag deviation at 9-Oct-94 in the Pwll Du area was
# 4.2 degrees (data from OS sheet 161, 1991).

# The data. Include as many notes as possible.
# Use		For
# ============  ==============================================
# -		Omitted clinometer reading.
# -		Omit bearing on plumbed legs.
# H, Horizontal Horizontal clinometer readings
# V, Vertical   Vertical clinometer readings
# U, Up		Plumbed legs with bearing omitted (clino not used)
# D, Down       Plumbed legs with bearing omitted (clino not used)
# +/-90		Vertical legs that were measured with a clinometer
# Data ordering (LRUD data may be entered but will be ignored)

centreline
